new file mode 100644
index 0000000..44f2810
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/controller-lease.md
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+# Controller lease protocol
+
+TCP 8765 remains ASCII lines with only `OK\n` or `ERROR\n` responses.
+No game state is returned. Existing controller tokens retain their meaning.
+Lines are limited to 127 bytes plus newline; invalid ASCII closes the connection.
+
+The first accepted controller command, or `LEASE`, claims exclusive control for
+that connection. Each accepted controller command and `LEASE` renews a fixed
+one-second monotonic lease. `LEASE` changes no controls. Renew at least every
+200–300 ms while the gameplay execution path is progressing. Never renew from
+an unrelated supervisor or autonomous heartbeat thread.
+
+The independent launcher deadman checks every 25 ms, independently of socket
+reads, writes, the UI loop and Charlie. Expiration neutralizes all sticks, hats,
+triggers and buttons. The expired connection cannot acquire/renew controls again;
+close it, reconnect, and compute fresh intent. Blank, partial, malformed, rejected,
+menu, player-selection and QUIT traffic cannot renew the lease. Existing 100 ms
+button taps remain synchronous; watchdog scheduling can be delayed by a tap
+holding the lease lock, plus operating-system scheduling. This is not a hard
+real-time or hardware watchdog. A frozen launcher/kernel or failed uinput output
+requires the independent operator stop path.
+
+Other connections receive ERROR for controller commands/renewals while an owner
+exists. A non-owner disconnect no longer releases the owner's controls.
+NEUTRAL is always allowed globally and releases ownership, including from an
+expired client or during a supervised qualification session. Owner disconnect
+releases immediately. Repeated neutral releases are safe. Failed neutral writes
+inhibit subsequent actuation, are logged, and are retried by the watchdog;
+successful physical release is never inferred from a failed write.
+
+Legacy clients need no negotiation for ordinary command sequences. Silence
+longer than one second now releases held controls; there is no unsafe unlimited
+hold compatibility mode. Charlie's native trial runner must require `LEASE`
+support and renew from gameplay execute(), including when positions are unchanged.
+
+Install the new module through the extended stopped-service
+`scripts/install_rom_intake.py`; post-install preflight checks its exact hash.
+The fresh-machine installer also copies it, but must never be rerun on an existing
+appliance. Preserve installed state and follow the guarded native handoff before
+any service stop/start. Source changes do not activate the watchdog.
